Solve this finite optimization problem exactly. Return one JSON object, without Markdown fences. Do not use external facts. Schedule every non-preemptive job at a nonnegative integer start. Intervals are half-open [start,start+duration). A job must start at or after release and finish at or before deadline and horizon. It must start at or after all jobs in after finish. Each resource demand applies throughout its entire interval; total simultaneous demand cannot exceed capacity. A job's interval must not overlap any of its own blocked intervals; an endpoint touching is allowed. Minimize makespan_multiplier * max(completion times) + sum(weight * completion time). Any optimum is acceptable.
For a feasible instance return {"status":"optimal","starts":{every_job:integer,...},"objective":integer,"checks":{"completion_times":{every_job:integer,...},"makespan":integer,"weighted_completion":integer},"explanation":"short explanation"}.
